# Build products and derived data: the whole tree is 1.6 GB and every byte of the
# excluded stuff can be regenerated (build.sh / build_db scripts) or is downloaded input.
# out/* rather than out/ so the one file the verification entry point needs can be
# re-included below (git cannot un-ignore anything inside an ignored directory).
out/*
!out/verify_search.py
app/build/
repo/
pydict/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Binary artifacts. The apk is reproducible from source + db; keep the shipped copies on
# /sdcard/Download instead of in history.
*.apk
*.db
*.db.gz
*.db.bak*
# Exception, and it has to sit below *.db.gz to win (last matching pattern decides):
# the shipped database, compressed, IS versioned (67 MB). Without it a clone cannot build an
# apk at all, because regenerating it needs repo/ + pydict/ + /root/anno/anno.ndjson
# (272 MB, and the anno corpus has no upstream source to re-download). `bash app/build.sh`
# takes this file straight to assets/ when out/poetry_lite.db is absent.
# From scratch instead: README 重建路径.
!out/poetry_lite.db.gz

# Signing identity. Deliberately NOT versioned: build.sh carries the password in plaintext
# and this repo gets copied around, so committing the keystore would publish the key.
# Losing it means every future install must uninstall the old app first (same signature
# required for upgrades), so there are two copies outside this tree:
#   /sdcard/Download/release.keystore   (device storage)
#   /root/backup/release.keystore       (host side)
release.keystore
*.keystore
*.jks

# Scratch
*.log
/tmp/
# Downloaded upstream corpus archive; the unpacked tree lives in repo/ (also ignored).
repo.tar.gz
